   "role": "greeting",
   "phrasing": "greet_02"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "I'm good, thanks.",
   "est_sec": 1.03,
   "gap_before": 0.34,
   "event": "greeting_answer",
   "phrasing": "greet_ans_01"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "I've got ADHD and studying normal ways just doesn't work for me.",
   "est_sec": 3.82,
   "gap_before": 0.54,
   "block": "studying.dlg9",
   "event": "ordinary_request"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "That makes sense. Lots of standard advice isn't built for how your brain works. What helps you focus, even a little?",
   "est_sec": 6.61,
   "gap_before": 0.9,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "studying.dlg9"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Weirdly, noise. And moving around.",
   "est_sec": 1.65,
   "gap_before": 1.56,
   "block": "studying.dlg9",
   "event": "ordinary_request"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Then lean into that. Try studying in a cafe, or with background sound, and take short walking breaks every twenty minutes.",
   "est_sec": 6.61,
   "gap_before": 0.48,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "studying.dlg9"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Twenty minutes feels short.",
   "est_sec": 1.34,
   "gap_before": 2.95,
   "block": "studying.dlg9",
   "event": "ordinary_request"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Short is good. Lots of quick wins keep your motivation going. You could also stand up while you read or use a whiteboard.",
   "est_sec": 7.23,
   "gap_before": 0.51,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "studying.dlg9"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "My teachers always told me",
   "est_sec": 1.65,
   "gap_before": 1.47,
   "event": "distractor",
   "kind": "pause",
   "block": "studying.dlg9"
  },
  {
